  "declaration": "PBPSGibbsSurvivalWork98.finite_energy_balance",
  "checks": [
    {
      "topic": "generic local-to-global contract",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "The assumptions are precisely integrability of f and g on each oriented adjacent interval and an energy increment identity on that interval. The conclusion produces their whole-endpoint integrability and the telescoped energy increment. It does not assume the global conclusion or add actual-source public providers."
    },
    {
      "topic": "zero case",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "For n=0 both endpoint indices in Fin1 are zero, so u_last-u0=0 and both interval integrals vanish. IntervalIntegrable.refl applies to arbitrary f,g without measurability premises. hf,hg,hstep have empty Fin0 domains."
    },
    {
      "topic": "successor index transport",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "The induction hypothesis restricts a,u to castSucc indices of the longer grid. Local assumptions likewise use j.castSucc; Fin.succ_castSucc identifies the adjoining right endpoints. The last interval is obtained at Fin.last n. Fin.succ_last and Fin.castSucc_zero identify the final and initial endpoints. There is no omitted interval or shifted first energy."
    },
    {
      "topic": "whole integrability without monotonicity",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IntervalIntegrable.trans combines the prefix and final interval for each function. The pinned API has no a<=b<=c requirement: it uses containment in the union of oriented interval supports. Thus repeated, descending and zigzag grid values are supported."
    },
    {
      "topic": "oriented adjacent integral addition and sign",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "The pinned integral_add_adjacent_intervals requires only the two integrability hypotheses. Writing Fpre+Flast=Ftotal and Gpre+Glast=Gtotal, hstep gives Flast-Glast=u_final-u_mid, while the induction conclusion gives Fpre-Gpre=u_mid-u0. Linear arithmetic yields u_final-u0=Ftotal-Gtotal with the stated sign."
    },
    {
      "topic": "repeated/reversed endpoints",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "A repeated adjacent endpoint forces its hstep energy increment to zero; no unsupported continuity of u is inferred. Reversed intervals use the signed interval integral. If the entire grid returns to its starting time, the assumptions force the telescoped energy increment to zero. These follow from the same general algebra, not from implicit time ordering."
    },
    {
      "topic": "actual98 boundary",
      "verdict": "PASS_WITH_UNDISCHARGED_ACTUAL_ADAPTER",
      "reason": "This helper has generic a,u,f,g and no actual Phi/Gamma physics. The wrapper must instantiate the n+2 actual time grid, establish both per-arc integrabilities, and derive hstep from actual arc FTC plus bounce U-invariance and actual endpoint energies. No incomplete Assembly98 was read or approved."
    }
  ],
